<title>JAPAN: Tokyo oil products market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo oil products market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo oil products market is closed for a national holiday on Thursday.</p>
<p>Trade will resume on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, naphtha prices jumped due to overnight crude rallies as well as brisk demand for near-term cargoes.</p>
<p>Open-spec naphtha for first-half June was quoted at $239.00/240.50 per tonne, up from Tuesday's $234.00/234.75.</p>
